        "display": "would swim",
        "explain": "The result of an imaginary situation: would + base verb, ‘would swim’."
      },
      {
        "use": "Imaginary present",
        "before": "If my brother",
        "after": "the answer, he’d tell us.",
        "hint": "(know)",
        "answers": [
          "knew"
        ],
        "display": "knew",
        "explain": "‘Know’ is irregular: the past simple is ‘knew’. It means he doesn’t know now."
      },
      {
        "use": "Imaginary present",
        "before": "If she",
        "after": "Japanese, she’d work in Tokyo.",
        "hint": "(speak)",
